      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Blaine''' is a city located in [[Grainger County, Tennessee]], [[USA]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 1,585.

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-Blaine.PNG|right|Location of Blaine, Tennessee]]
Blaine is located at 36&amp;deg;9'3&quot; North, 83&amp;deg;42'2&quot; West (36.150854, -83.700443){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 22.8 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (8.8 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  22.8 km&amp;sup2; (8.8 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of the area is covered with water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 1,585 people, 636 households, and 478 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 69.4/km&amp;sup2; (179.6/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 680 housing units at an average density of 29.8/km&amp;sup2; (77.1/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 96.91% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 1.07% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.32% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.13% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.63% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.95% from two or more races.  1.01% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 636 households out of which 31.4% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 60.2% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 10.4% have a female householder with no husband present, and 24.7% are non-families. 20.4% of all households are made up of individuals and 5.2% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.49 and the average family size is 2.87.

In the city the population is spread out with 22.5% under the age of 18, 9.5% from 18 to 24, 30.8% from 25 to 44, 26.4% from 45 to 64, and 10.8% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 37 years.  For every 100 females there are 95.2 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 95.2 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $30,677, and the median income for a family is $35,417. Males have a median income of $26,213 versus $20,707 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $16,587.  14.9% of the population and 11.7% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 19.9% of those under the age of 18 and 27.1% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

