      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Baileyton''' is a town located in [[Greene County, Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 504.

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-Baileyton.PNG|right|Location of Baileyton, Tennessee]]
Baileyton is located at 36&amp;deg;19'41&quot; North, 82&amp;deg;49'50&quot; West (36.328094, -82.830501){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 3.7 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (1.4 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  3.7 km&amp;sup2; (1.4 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of the area is covered with water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 504 people, 237 households, and 138 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 136.1/km&amp;sup2; (353.6/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 275 housing units at an average density of 74.3/km&amp;sup2; (192.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 98.21% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.99% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.20% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.00% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.40% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.20% from two or more races.  0.79% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 237 households out of which 23.6% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 44.7% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 12.2% have a female householder with no husband present, and 41.4% are non-families. 36.3% of all households are made up of individuals and 15.2% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.13 and the average family size is 2.77.

In the town the population is spread out with 19.0% under the age of 18, 8.7% from 18 to 24, 25.4% from 25 to 44, 29.6% from 45 to 64, and 17.3% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 42 years.  For every 100 females there are 88.1 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 83.8 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $20,139, and the median income for a family is $34,375. Males have a median income of $26,389 versus $18,056 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $12,410.  20.4% of the population and 13.1% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 26.0% of those under the age of 18 and 25.9% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

