      <timestamp>2006-02-25T22:12:01Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <ip>129.59.46.194</ip>
      </contributor>
      <comment>/* Famous Residents */</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Greeneville''' is a town located in [[Greene County, Tennessee|Greene County]], [[Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 15,198.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Greene County, Tennessee|Greene County]]{{GR|6}}. The town was named in honor of [[Nathanael Greene]]; incidentally, it is the only ''Greeneville'' in the [[United States]] to  have kept the true spelling &amp;mdash; the other ''Greenvilles'' dropped the trailing ''e''.

[[USS Greeneville (SSN-772)|USS Greeneville]] is named in honor of this town.

The town hosts the [[Greeneville Astros]] baseball club of the [[Appalachian League]].

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-Greeneville.PNG|right|Location of Greeneville, Tennessee]]
Greeneville is located at 36&amp;deg;10'6&quot; North, 82&amp;deg;49'21&quot; West (36.168240, -82.822474){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 36.4 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (14.0 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  36.4 km&amp;sup2; (14.0 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of the area is covered with water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 15,198 people, 6,641 households, and 4,097 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 417.9/km&amp;sup2; (1,082.4/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 7,212 housing units at an average density of 198.3/km&amp;sup2; (513.6/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 92.03% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 5.74% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.19% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.54% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.02% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.88% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.60% from two or more races.  1.49% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 6,641 households out of which 25.5% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 44.6% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 13.9% have a female householder with no husband present, and 38.3% are non-families. 34.5% of all households are made up of individuals and 16.1% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.18 and the average family size is 2.78.

In the town the population is spread out with 21.3% under the age of 18, 7.7% from 18 to 24, 26.3% from 25 to 44, 24.3% from 45 to 64, and 20.4% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 41 years.  For every 100 females there are 84.4 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 79.5 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $25,999, and the median income for a family is $36,129. Males have a median income of $30,629 versus $21,425 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $17,126.  20.7% of the population and 16.5% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 28.5% of those under the age of 18 and 18.0% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

The [[Los Angeles class submarine|''Los Angeles''-class submarine]] [[USS Greeneville (SSN-772)|''Greeneville'' (SSN-772)]] was named in honor of this city.


==Famous Residents==
*[[Andrew Johnson]]: Mayor of Greeneville, Tennessee. U.S. Senator, U.S. Vice President, U.S. Presdient
*Scott Niswonger, proprieter of LandAir, a trucking company
*Allen Johnson - NHRA Pro Stock Driver
*Bradley Max Smith - Writer
*Cameron Judd - Writer

== External links ==
[http://www.itropolisinc.com/greenville/index.htm Official town website]
{{Mapit-US-cityscale|36.16824|-82.822474}}
{{Tennessee}}
