== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 1,749 people, 742 households, and 532 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 159.3/km&amp;sup2; (413.0/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 805 housing units at an average density of 73.3/km&amp;sup2; (190.1/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 98.80% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.46% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.00% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.11% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.00% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.63% from two or more races.  0.11% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 742 households out of which 28.8% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 57.8% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 10.1% have a female householder with no husband present, and 28.3% are non-families. 25.1% of all households are made up of individuals and 10.0% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.36 and the average family size is 2.78.

In the town the population is spread out with 20.8% under the age of 18, 6.9% from 18 to 24, 28.8% from 25 to 44, 28.3% from 45 to 64, and 15.2% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 41 years.  For every 100 females there are 92.8 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 90.2 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $29,194, and the median income for a family is $36,118. Males have a median income of $26,211 versus $19,479 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $16,243.  8.8% of the population and 5.7% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 6.5% of those under the age of 18 and 19.0% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

