      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Beersheba Springs''' is a town located in [[Grundy County, Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 553.

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-BeershebaSprings.PNG|right|Location of BeershebaSprings, Tennessee]]
Beersheba Springs is located at 35&amp;deg;28'2&quot; North, 85&amp;deg;40'18&quot; West (35.467209, -85.671700){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 12.7 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (4.9 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  12.7 km&amp;sup2; (4.9 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of the area is covered with water.

Also, Beersheba Springs is a very scenic area. It has a lot of places to go hiking and such. Stone Door is a great place for hiking. It has a great view at the end of the hike.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 553 people, 232 households, and 168 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 43.5/km&amp;sup2; (112.6/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 304 housing units at an average density of 23.9/km&amp;sup2; (61.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 99.82% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.00% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.00% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.00% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.00% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.18% from two or more races.  0.54% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 232 households out of which 28.0% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 59.5% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 10.8% have a female householder with no husband present, and 27.2% are non-families. 23.7% of all households are made up of individuals and 9.5% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.38 and the average family size is 2.82.

In the town the population is spread out with 21.7% under the age of 18, 7.2% from 18 to 24, 26.0% from 25 to 44, 26.8% from 45 to 64, and 18.3% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 42 years.  For every 100 females there are 94.0 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 95.0 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $22,045, and the median income for a family is $26,250. Males have a median income of $27,083 versus $20,000 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $13,691.  32.5% of the population and 26.9% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 38.8% of those under the age of 18 and 26.4% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

