    <title>Harrison, Tennessee</title>
    <id>135208</id>
    <revision>
      <id>27895518</id>
      <timestamp>2005-11-10T05:37:44Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>ScribeOfTheNile</username>
        <id>81807</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>dab</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Harrison''' is a [[census-designated place]] located in [[Hamilton County, Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the CDP had a total population of 7,630.
Prior to the [[Tennessee Valley Authority]]'s [[Chickamauga Dam]], Harrison was the [[County seat|seat]] of Hamilton County. The old city was flooded, as portrayed in the 1960 movie [[&quot;Wild River.&quot;]] The Hamilton County Landfill is located in Harrison, as well as Bear Trace, a Jack Nicklaus-designed golf course, and Skull Island, a recreational area owned by [[TVA]].

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-Harrison.PNG|right|Location of Harrison, Tennessee]]
Harrison is located at 35&amp;deg;7'9&quot; North, 85&amp;deg;8'58&quot; West (35.119296, -85.149487){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the CDP has a total area of 23.7 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (9.1 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  18.9 km&amp;sup2; (7.3 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 4.8 km&amp;sup2; (1.9 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 20.33% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 7,630 people, 2,856 households, and 2,281 families residing in the CDP.  The [[population density]] is 404.1/km&amp;sup2; (1,046.0/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 2,956 housing units at an average density of 156.6/km&amp;sup2; (405.2/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the CDP is 84.59% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 12.94% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.35% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.69% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.01% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.26% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.15% from two or more races.  1.17% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 2,856 households out of which 35.0% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 65.8% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 10.6% have a female householder with no husband present, and 20.1% are non-families. 16.6% of all households are made up of individuals and 5.1% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.67 and the average family size is 3.00.

In the CDP the population is spread out with 24.9% under the age of 18, 7.8% from 18 to 24, 29.9% from 25 to 44, 27.4% from 45 to 64, and 9.9% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 38 years.  For every 100 females there are 93.8 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 92.0 males.

The median income for a household in the CDP is $49,393, and the median income for a family is $55,412. Males have a median income of $35,332 versus $27,487 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the CDP is $22,893.  3.1% of the population and 1.7% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 1.4% of those under the age of 18 and 6.7% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== Education ==
The [[Hamilty County School System]] operates five schools in this area(Snow Hill Elementary School, Harrison Elementary School, Brown Middle School, Central High School, and Hamilton County High School.)
