      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Lookout Mountain''' is a town located in [[Hamilton County, Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 2,000.

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-LookoutMountain.PNG|right|Location of Lookout Mountain, Tennessee]]
Lookout Mountain is located at 34&amp;deg;59'47&quot; North, 85&amp;deg;21'3&quot; West (34.996442, -85.350810){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 3.3 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (1.3 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  3.3 km&amp;sup2; (1.3 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of the area is covered with water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 2,000 people, 791 households, and 586 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 612.9/km&amp;sup2; (1,587.6/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 836 housing units at an average density of 256.2/km&amp;sup2; (663.6/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 96.90% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 2.10% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.05% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.50% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.10% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.05% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.30% from two or more races.  0.40% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 791 households out of which 35.3% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 66.9% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 6.3% have a female householder with no husband present, and 25.9% are non-families. 24.5% of all households are made up of individuals and 13.3% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.53 and the average family size is 3.03.

In the town the population is spread out with 28.1% under the age of 18, 4.3% from 18 to 24, 21.1% from 25 to 44, 27.6% from 45 to 64, and 19.0% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 43 years.  For every 100 females there are 90.8 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 85.8 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $100,782, and the median income for a family is $121,037. Males have a median income of $94,501 versus $37,917 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $60,938.  4.2% of the population and 4.3% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 1.6% of those under the age of 18 and 2.1% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

