      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Ooltewah''' ({{audio|en-us-Ooltewah.ogg|hear it}}) is a [[census-designated place]] located in [[Hamilton County, Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the CDP had a total population of 5,681.  At one point it was the county seat of James County, a former Tennessee county which went [[bankruptcy|bankrupt]] and was subsequently distributed to the surrounding counties.  The former James County Courthouse located in on the square in downtown Ooltewah is the town's major landmark.

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-Ooltewah.PNG|right|Location of Ooltewah, Tennessee]]
Ooltewah is located at 35&amp;deg;4'1&quot; North, 85&amp;deg;4'53&quot; West (35.066834, -85.081421){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the CDP has a total area of 19.8 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (7.7 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  19.8 km&amp;sup2; (7.7 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of the area is covered with water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 5,681 people, 2,153 households, and 1,619 families residing in the CDP.  The [[population density]] is 286.4/km&amp;sup2; (741.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 2,290 housing units at an average density of 115.4/km&amp;sup2; (298.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the CDP is 83.49% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 11.93% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.46% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.84% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.02% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 1.13% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 2.13% from two or more races.  1.94% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 2,153 households out of which 32.7% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 59.6% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 11.6% have a female householder with no husband present, and 24.8% are non-families. 20.3% of all households are made up of individuals and 5.3% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.62 and the average family size is 3.04.

In the CDP the population is spread out with 25.2% under the age of 18, 8.8% from 18 to 24, 30.4% from 25 to 44, 25.9% from 45 to 64, and 9.7% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 36 years.  For every 100 females there are 97.8 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 94.0 males.

The median income for a household in the CDP is $42,243, and the median income for a family is $46,439. Males have a median income of $33,423 versus $23,036 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the CDP is $23,034.  7.6% of the population and 4.6% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 9.0% of those under the age of 18 and 7.8% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

