      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Red Bank''' is a city located in [[Hamilton County, Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 12,418.  Red Bank is an [[enclave]]; its area is completely surrounded by that of [[Chattanooga, Tennessee|Chattanooga]].

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-RedBank.PNG|right|Location of Red Bank, Tennessee]]
Red Bank is located at 35&amp;deg;6'37&quot; North, 85&amp;deg;17'49&quot; West (35.110372, -85.297048){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 16.7 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (6.4 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  16.7 km&amp;sup2; (6.4 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of the area is covered with water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 12,418 people, 5,897 households, and 3,290 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 744.5/km&amp;sup2; (1,927.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 6,443 housing units at an average density of 386.3/km&amp;sup2; (1,000.3/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 87.61% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 8.24% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.52% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.89% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.06% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 1.19% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.51% from two or more races.  2.83% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 5,897 households out of which 22.8% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 39.2% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 12.6% have a female householder with no husband present, and 44.2% are non-families. 37.9% of all households are made up of individuals and 11.8% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.10 and the average family size is 2.77.

In the city the population is spread out with 20.0% under the age of 18, 11.3% from 18 to 24, 31.3% from 25 to 44, 22.0% from 45 to 64, and 15.4% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 36 years.  For every 100 females there are 91.1 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 87.3 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $33,848, and the median income for a family is $41,696. Males have a median income of $30,832 versus $24,708 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $18,877.  8.0% of the population and 5.1% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 7.9% of those under the age of 18 and 6.2% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== External links ==
{{Mapit-US-cityscale|35.110372|-85.297048}}

