      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Walden''' is a town located in [[Hamilton County, Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 1,960.

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-Walden.PNG|right|Location of Walden, Tennessee]]
Walden is located at 35&amp;deg;9'40&quot; North, 85&amp;deg;18'44&quot; West (35.161154, -85.312116){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 9.4 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (3.6 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  9.4 km&amp;sup2; (3.6 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of the area is covered with water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 1,960 people, 728 households, and 583 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 208.5/km&amp;sup2; (539.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 776 housing units at an average density of 82.5/km&amp;sup2; (213.6/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 99.13% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.00% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.20% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.36% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.15% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.15% from two or more races.  0.77% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 728 households out of which 35.4% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 71.2% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 7.0% have a female householder with no husband present, and 19.8% are non-families. 17.6% of all households are made up of individuals and 6.7% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.69 and the average family size is 3.06.

In the town the population is spread out with 28.0% under the age of 18, 5.3% from 18 to 24, 25.7% from 25 to 44, 28.9% from 45 to 64, and 12.1% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 40 years.  For every 100 females there are 98.0 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 94.6 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $68,977, and the median income for a family is $75,919. Males have a median income of $60,074 versus $27,083 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $37,287.  4.6% of the population and 4.9% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 4.5% of those under the age of 18 and 3.8% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

