      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Rogersville''' is a town located in [[Hawkins County, Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 4,240.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Hawkins County, Tennessee|Hawkins County]]{{GR|6}}.

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-Rogersville.PNG|right|Location of Rogersville, Tennessee]]
Rogersville is located at 36&amp;deg;24'52&quot; North, 82&amp;deg;59'51&quot; West (36.414418, -82.997466){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 8.6 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (3.3 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  8.6 km&amp;sup2; (3.3 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of the area is covered with water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 4,240 people, 2,060 households, and 1,155 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 493.1/km&amp;sup2; (1,277.0/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 2,268 housing units at an average density of 263.8/km&amp;sup2; (683.1/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 94.13% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 4.06% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.14% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.31% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.02% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.66% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.68% from two or more races.  1.06% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 2,060 households out of which 21.0% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 38.9% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 14.2% have a female householder with no husband present, and 43.9% are non-families. 40.9% of all households are made up of individuals and 21.1% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 1.97 and the average family size is 2.63.

In the town the population is spread out with 17.8% under the age of 18, 8.0% from 18 to 24, 23.2% from 25 to 44, 24.8% from 45 to 64, and 26.2% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 46 years.  For every 100 females there are 76.6 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 72.1 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $23,275, and the median income for a family is $32,236. Males have a median income of $30,226 versus $22,482 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $16,940.  21.0% of the population and 14.9% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 30.0% of those under the age of 18 and 15.8% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== Schools ==
* [http://www.hawkinsschools.net/cherokee Cherokee High School]; mascot is the Chief
* [http://www.hawkinsschools.net/rms Rogersville Middle School] (formally Rogersville High School); mascot is the Warrior
* [http://www.rcschool.net Rogersville City School]; mascot is also the Warrior
* [http://www.hawkinsschools.net/hes Hawkins Elementary School]; mascot is the Bearcat
* [http://www.hawkinsschools.net/jrp/ Joesph Rogers Primary School]; mascot is the Bobcat

==Culture==
