    <title>Paris, Tennessee</title>
    <id>135242</id>
    <revision>
      <id>39188856</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-11T09:16:48Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Leslie Mateus</username>
        <id>242123</id>
      </contributor>
      <comment>/* External links */ +pt</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">[[Image:ParisTNEiffel.jpg|thumb|250px|right|The replica of the [[Eiffel tower]] in Paris, Tennessee.]]
'''Paris''' is a town located in [[Henry County, Tennessee]], 86 miles (138 km) west of [[Nashville, Tennessee|Nashville]], on a fork of the [[West Sandy River]].  In [[1900]], 2,018 people lived in Paris, Tennessee; in [[1910]], 3,881; and in [[1940]], 6,395.As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total [[population]] of 9,763.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Henry County, Tennessee|Henry County]]{{GR|6}}.

A small replica of the [[Eiffel Tower]] stands in a park in Paris. 

Paris is also home of the &quot;World's Biggest Fish Fry&quot;.  The festival is held every year and culminates on a weekend, usually in late April, with a parade, an art and craft fair, a [[rodeo]] and a [[fun fair]].  There is a sign which features a roughly 20' long artificial [[catfish]] that can be seen when entering the town from the south on U.S. Highway 79.

[[Image:Catfish welcome to paris tennessee.jpg|thumb|250px|right|The artificial [[catfish]], sign underneth reads ''Welcome to Paris, Tennessee''.]]

== Geography ==
Paris is located at 36&amp;deg;18'4&quot; North, 88&amp;deg;18'50&quot; West (36.301229, -88.313815){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 28.3 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (10.9 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  28.2 km&amp;sup2; (10.9 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.1 km&amp;sup2; (0.04 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is [[water]].  The total area is 0.37% water.
[[Image:TNMap-doton-Paris.PNG|thumb|right|300px|Location of Paris on a map of the state of [[Tennessee]].]]
== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 9,763 people, 4,394 households, and 2,605 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 346.5/km&amp;sup2; (897.4/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 4,965 housing units at an average density of 176.2/km&amp;sup2; (456.4/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 77.09% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 20.26% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.10% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.60% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.06% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.39% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.50% from two or more races.  1.18% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 4,394 households out of which 24.8% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 38.5% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 16.8% have a female householder with no husband present, and 40.7% are non-families. 36.8% of all households are made up of individuals and 19.3% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.14 and the average family size is 2.77.

In the city the population is spread out with 21.7% under the age of 18, 8.5% from 18 to 24, 25.0% from 25 to 44, 22.4% from 45 to 64, and 22.4% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 41 years.  For every 100 females there are 81.5 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 77.1 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $25,261, and the median income for a family is $32,258. Males have a median income of $27,759 versus $20,198 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $15,572.  19.0% of the population and 14.1% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 26.6% of those under the age of 18 and 20.5% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

==Famous People from Paris, Tennessee==
*Vernon Jarrett, newspaper columnist and social commentator
*[[Bobby Jones]], gospel singer
*[[Cherry Jones]], [[Tony Award]]-winning actress
*Ula Love, permormer in the [[Ziegfield Follies]]
*Harry Neal, member of piano duo [[Nelson &amp; Neal]]
*[[Hank Williams, Jr.]], country music singer
*[[Howell Edmunds Jackson]], U.S. Supreme Court Justice

== External links ==
*{{Mapit-US-cityscale|36.301229|-88.313815}}
*[http://www.paris.tn.org/index.htm Official town web site]
*[http://www.paris.tn.org/fishschedule2001.htm World's Biggest Fish Fry]

{{Tennessee}}

