== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 667 people, 284 households, and 191 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 283.0/km&amp;sup2; (730.0/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 328 housing units at an average density of 139.2/km&amp;sup2; (359.0/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 95.65% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 2.70% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.15% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.45% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.45% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.60% from two or more races.  0.75% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 284 households out of which 26.8% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 53.9% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 9.5% have a female householder with no husband present, and 32.7% are non-families. 27.5% of all households are made up of individuals and 14.1% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.27 and the average family size is 2.73.

In the city the population is spread out with 19.8% under the age of 18, 8.7% from 18 to 24, 26.8% from 25 to 44, 22.9% from 45 to 64, and 21.7% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 41 years.  For every 100 females there are 92.2 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 91.1 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $28,750, and the median income for a family is $36,042. Males have a median income of $22,315 versus $20,481 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $17,131.  10.8% of the population and 7.4% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 24.3% of those under the age of 18 and 9.3% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

