      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Mountain City''' is a town located in [[Johnson County, Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 2,383.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Johnson County, Tennessee|Johnson County]]{{GR|6}}.

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-MountainCity.PNG|right|Location of Mountain City, Tennessee]]
Mountain City is located at 36&amp;deg;28'6&quot; North, 81&amp;deg;48'14&quot; West (36.468444, -81.803856){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 8.6 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (3.3 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  8.6 km&amp;sup2; (3.3 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of the area is covered with water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 2,383 people, 1,136 households, and 664 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 278.0/km&amp;sup2; (720.8/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 1,250 housing units at an average density of 145.8/km&amp;sup2; (378.1/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 97.86% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.92% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.25% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.25% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.29% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.42% from two or more races.  0.80% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 1,136 households out of which 22.4% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 42.3% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 12.5% have a female householder with no husband present, and 41.5% are non-families. 38.3% of all households are made up of individuals and 18.9% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.05 and the average family size is 2.71.

In the town the population is spread out with 19.2% under the age of 18, 7.0% from 18 to 24, 26.4% from 25 to 44, 26.7% from 45 to 64, and 20.7% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 43 years.  For every 100 females there are 89.3 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 83.9 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $16,587, and the median income for a family is $31,406. Males have a median income of $26,042 versus $19,145 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $17,202.  27.1% of the population and 21.6% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 37.4% of those under the age of 18 and 20.6% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== External links ==
