      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Halls''' is a town located in [[Lauderdale County, Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 2,311. It is home to the Army Air Museum, which documents the history of the WWII Army Air Corp. It was the main base for the [[B-17]] Bombers in the mid 40's.

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-Halls.PNG|right|Location of Halls, Tennessee]]
Halls is located at 35&amp;deg;52'50&quot; North, 89&amp;deg;23'60&quot; West (35.880612, -89.399974){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 9.5 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (3.7 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  9.5 km&amp;sup2; (3.7 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.27% is water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 2,311 people, 946 households, and 642 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 243.8/km&amp;sup2; (630.8/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 1,051 housing units at an average density of 110.9/km&amp;sup2; (286.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 70.45% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 28.13% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.48% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.09% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.04% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.17% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.65% from two or more races.  0.65% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 946 households out of which 29.7% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 45.3% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 17.7% have a female householder with no husband present, and 32.1% are non-families. 30.0% of all households are made up of individuals and 15.9% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.44 and the average family size is 3.03.

In the town the population is spread out with 26.7% under the age of 18, 7.7% from 18 to 24, 26.8% from 25 to 44, 22.3% from 45 to 64, and 16.4% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 37 years.  For every 100 females there are 87.1 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 81.8 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $24,142, and the median income for a family is $29,063. Males have a median income of $26,528 versus $19,300 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $15,011.  23.3% of the population and 21.8% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 29.2% of those under the age of 18 and 29.0% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

