      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Loudon''' is a town located in [[Loudon County, Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 4,476.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Loudon County, Tennessee|Loudon County]]{{GR|6}}.

Loudon is located in eastern Tennessee, southwest of [[Knoxville, Tennessee|Knoxville]], near the [[Fort Loudoun Dam]], at the junction of the [[Tennessee River|Tennessee]] and [[Little Tennessee River]]s. 

[[Fort Loudoun (Tennessee)|Fort Loudoun]], which was built in [[1756]], and fell to the [[Cherokee]] in [[1760]], is nearby in [[Monroe County, Tennessee|Monroe County]].

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-Loudon.PNG|right|Location of Loudon, Tennessee]]
Loudon is located at 35&amp;deg;44'2&quot; North, 84&amp;deg;20'58&quot; West (35.733856, -84.349417){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 25.0 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (9.6 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  24.1 km&amp;sup2; (9.3 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.9 km&amp;sup2; (0.3 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 3.42% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 4,476 people, 1,858 households, and 1,202 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 185.4/km&amp;sup2; (480.3/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 2,007 housing units at an average density of 83.1/km&amp;sup2; (215.4/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 92.98% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 3.22% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.31% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.38% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 2.03% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.07% from two or more races.  3.24% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 1,858 households out of which 27.5% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 49.0% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 12.3% have a female householder with no husband present, and 35.3% are non-families. 31.3% of all households are made up of individuals and 16.3% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.29 and the average family size is 2.85.

In the town the population is spread out with 21.3% under the age of 18, 7.6% from 18 to 24, 26.3% from 25 to 44, 22.6% from 45 to 64, and 22.3% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 42 years.  For every 100 females there are 84.8 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 80.6 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $30,108, and the median income for a family is $39,410. Males have a median income of $31,229 versus $20,611 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $16,501.  17.1% of the population and 10.7% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 24.4% of those under the age of 18 and 15.3% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

