      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Kimball''' is a town located in [[Marion County, Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 1,312.

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-Kimball.PNG|right|Location of Kimball, Tennessee]]
Kimball is located at 35&amp;deg;2'49&quot; North, 85&amp;deg;40'28&quot; West (35.046956, -85.674476){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 12.8 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (4.9 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  12.8 km&amp;sup2; (4.9 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of the area is covered with water.

== History ==
Originally founded in [[1890]] as a model industrial city by [[Hanniball Kimball]] with support of the British [[Anglo-American Company, Limited]].
The location was chosen to be similar to another planned city, [[Colorado Springs, Colorado|Colorado Springs]].
It was backed by mountains with three miles of frontage on the [[Tennessee River]] and rail connections on the [[Nashville, Chattanooga and St. Louis Railway]].
Unfortunately, soon after selling 321 lots the town president, [[Logan Roots]] left for England taking the money and the company failed.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 1,312 people, 563 households, and 389 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 102.5/km&amp;sup2; (265.6/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 607 housing units at an average density of 47.4/km&amp;sup2; (122.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 97.48% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.99% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.53% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.00% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.00% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.99% from two or more races.  0.08% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 563 households out of which 30.0% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 54.7% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 10.8% have a female householder with no husband present, and 30.9% are non-families. 29.1% of all households are made up of individuals and 11.4% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.33 and the average family size is 2.85.

In the town the population is spread out with 22.8% under the age of 18, 7.0% from 18 to 24, 29.0% from 25 to 44, 28.6% from 45 to 64, and 12.6% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 40 years.  For every 100 females there are 92.1 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 86.6 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $33,359, and the median income for a family is $41,094. Males have a median income of $31,141 versus $21,382 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $17,454.  9.0% of the population and 7.9% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 10.0% of those under the age of 18 and 8.4% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

