      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Lewisburg''' is a city located in [[Marshall County, Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 10,413.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Marshall County, Tennessee|Marshall County]]{{GR|6}}. Lewisburg is located in central Tennessee, south of [[Nashville, Tennessee|Nashville]].

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-Lewisburg.PNG|right|Location of Lewisburg, Tennessee]]
Lewisburg is located at 35&amp;deg;26'57&quot; North, 86&amp;deg;47'35&quot; West (35.449034, -86.793112){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 30.3 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (11.7 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  30.3 km&amp;sup2; (11.7 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.09% is water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 10,413 people, 4,242 households, and 2,740 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 344.2/km&amp;sup2; (891.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 4,584 housing units at an average density of 151.5/km&amp;sup2; (392.4/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 79.96% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 15.44% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.19% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.47% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.03% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 2.85% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.06% from two or more races.  5.15% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 4,242 households out of which 29.2% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 43.4% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 16.6% have a female householder with no husband present, and 35.4% are non-families. 31.0% of all households are made up of individuals and 13.7% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.38 and the average family size is 2.94.

In the city the population is spread out with 24.2% under the age of 18, 10.2% from 18 to 24, 27.3% from 25 to 44, 22.1% from 45 to 64, and 16.3% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 37 years.  For every 100 females there are 90.0 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 86.4 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $31,033, and the median income for a family is $38,246. Males have a median income of $30,619 versus $21,765 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $16,401.  16.1% of the population and 12.7% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 20.1% of those under the age of 18 and 14.2% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

