      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Athens''' is a [[city]] located in [[McMinn County, Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total [[population]] of 13,220.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[McMinn County, Tennessee|McMinn County]]{{GR|6}}.

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-Athens.PNG|right|Location of Athens, Tennessee]]
Athens is located at 35&amp;deg;26'53&quot; North, 84&amp;deg;36'7&quot; West (35.448171, -84.602069){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 35.1 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (13.5 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  35.1 km&amp;sup2; (13.5 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of the area is covered with [[water]].

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 13,220 people, 5,550 households, and 3,590 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 377.0/km&amp;sup2; (976.3/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 6,086 housing units at an average density of 173.5/km&amp;sup2; (449.4/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 86.33% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 9.32% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.23% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 1.38% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.07% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 1.34% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.33% from two or more races.  3.01% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 5,550 households out of which 30.0% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 47.2% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 14.8% have a female householder with no husband present, and 35.3% are non-families. 31.7% of all households are made up of individuals and 13.0% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.29 and the average family size is 2.89.

In the city the population is spread out with 23.9% under the age of 18, 10.1% from 18 to 24, 28.3% from 25 to 44, 21.4% from 45 to 64, and 16.3% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 36 years.  For every 100 females there are 84.8 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 80.2 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $29,277, and the median income for a family is $39,563. Males have a median income of $32,170 versus $20,917 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $16,877.  18.4% of the population and 14.6% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 22.6% of those under the age of 18 and 22.1% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

