      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Calhoun''' is a town located in [[McMinn County, Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 496.

On December 9, 1990, fog played havoc with the worst accident in Tennessee's history; 99 vehicles crashed on a strech of fog-prone Interstate 75 and was listed as the worst disaster in history.

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-Calhoun.PNG|right|Location of Calhoun, Tennessee]]
Calhoun is located at 35&amp;deg;17'45&quot; North, 84&amp;deg;44'53&quot; West (35.295712, -84.748027){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 2.8 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (1.1 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  2.6 km&amp;sup2; (1.0 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.1 km&amp;sup2; (0.1 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 4.67% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 496 people, 205 households, and 148 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 187.8/km&amp;sup2; (486.4/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 225 housing units at an average density of 85.2/km&amp;sup2; (220.6/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 97.78% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.81% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.00% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 1.01% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.00% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.40% from two or more races.  3.43% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 205 households out of which 28.3% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 60.0% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 7.8% have a female householder with no husband present, and 27.8% are non-families. 25.9% of all households are made up of individuals and 10.7% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.42 and the average family size is 2.86.

In the town the population is spread out with 22.6% under the age of 18, 6.0% from 18 to 24, 25.2% from 25 to 44, 29.2% from 45 to 64, and 16.9% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 41 years.  For every 100 females there are 101.6 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 93.9 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $38,438, and the median income for a family is $44,688. Males have a median income of $36,563 versus $20,333 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $19,984.  10.2% of the population and 5.3% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 3.5% of those under the age of 18 and 9.5% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

