      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Etowah''' is a city located in [[McMinn County, Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 3,663.

== History ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-Etowah.PNG|right|Location of Etowah, Tennessee]]
Etowah was founded in 1906, primarily as a location for a depot on the [[Louisville &amp; Nashville Railroad]] (L&amp;N) line as part of a more direct route between [[Atlanta, Georgia]] and [[Cincinnati, Ohio]].

== Geography ==
Etowah is located at 35&amp;deg;19'46&quot; North, 84&amp;deg;31'42&quot; West (35.329579, -84.528196){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 7.2 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (2.8 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  7.2 km&amp;sup2; (2.8 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of the area is covered with water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 3,663 people, 1,545 households, and 979 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 510.6/km&amp;sup2; (1,321.8/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 1,769 housing units at an average density of 246.6/km&amp;sup2; (638.4/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 93.42% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 3.25% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.38% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.11% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.08% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 1.09% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.67% from two or more races.  2.13% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 1,545 households out of which 26.6% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 47.5% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 12.5% have a female householder with no husband present, and 36.6% are non-families. 32.8% of all households are made up of individuals and 17.2% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.25 and the average family size is 2.86.

In the city the population is spread out with 21.4% under the age of 18, 7.4% from 18 to 24, 25.6% from 25 to 44, 22.4% from 45 to 64, and 23.2% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 42 years.  For every 100 females there are 85.1 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 80.5 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $28,117, and the median income for a family is $33,034. Males have a median income of $27,824 versus $18,882 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $15,298.  15.9% of the population and 7.4% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 27.6% of those under the age of 18 and 13.7% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

