      <contributor>
        <ip>160.36.81.16</ip>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Lobelville''' is a city located in [[Perry County, Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 915.

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-Lobelville.PNG|right|Location of Lobelville, Tennessee]]
Lobelville is located at 35&amp;deg;45'4&quot; North, 87&amp;deg;47'35&quot; West (35.751119, -87.793085){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 10.2 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (3.9 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  10.2 km&amp;sup2; (3.9 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.25% is water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 915 people, 400 households, and 261 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 89.7/km&amp;sup2; (232.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 464 housing units at an average density of 45.5/km&amp;sup2; (117.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 97.70% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.22% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.33% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.22% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.55% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.98% from two or more races.  0.55% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 400 households out of which 30.0% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 48.5% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 12.5% have a female householder with no husband present, and 34.8% are non-families. 31.8% of all households are made up of individuals and 17.0% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.29 and the average family size is 2.87.

In the city the population is spread out with 24.7% under the age of 18, 5.5% from 18 to 24, 27.5% from 25 to 44, 25.7% from 45 to 64, and 16.6% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 39 years.  For every 100 females there are 90.6 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 84.7 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $26,193, and the median income for a family is $31,389. Males have a median income of $28,750 versus $21,683 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $15,549.  19.8% of the population and 14.3% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 20.6% of those under the age of 18 and 12.6% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== History, Commerce, and Recreation ==

Lobelville was named after 18th century French fur trapper and explorer of the Buffalo River and Tennessee River valleys, Henri de Lobel.  Lobel established a trading fort on the Buffalo River around 1800 expecting that it would become a trading route. The close proximity of the Tennessee River made this an unprofitable venture, and it never took off as a major trading point.

Lobelville now is the site of a major transfer point on the Tennessee Gas Pipeline Company pipeline network and is bisected by State Route 13, a connector to Interstate 40 (via exit 143 approximately 10 miles north in Humphreys County, Tennessee) and Federal Highway 412.

The Buffalo River provides a substantial income of tourism through canoeing and fishing, as does the larger Tennessee River.  Moustail Landing State Park is situated south-west of Lobelville in Perry County along the Tennessee River.  Buffalo River Country Club is a local 9-hole semi-private golf course.  Hunting, fishing, and camping (both at prepared sites and back-country) are widely available  in the area.


