      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Dunlap''' is a city located in [[Sequatchie County, Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 4,173.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Sequatchie County, Tennessee|Sequatchie County]]{{GR|6}}.

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-Dunlap.PNG|right|Location of Dunlap, Tennessee]]
Dunlap is located at 35&amp;deg;22'38&quot; North, 85&amp;deg;23'18&quot; West (35.377236, -85.388455){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 22.3 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (8.6 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  22.3 km&amp;sup2; (8.6 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of the area is covered with water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 4,173 people, 1,642 households, and 1,182 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 186.9/km&amp;sup2; (484.2/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 1,767 housing units at an average density of 79.1/km&amp;sup2; (205.0/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 98.87% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.17% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.19% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.24% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.10% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.43% from two or more races.  0.81% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 1,642 households out of which 33.5% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 53.6% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 14.3% have a female householder with no husband present, and 28.0% are non-families. 25.3% of all households are made up of individuals and 10.9% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.47 and the average family size is 2.90.

In the city the population is spread out with 24.7% under the age of 18, 9.6% from 18 to 24, 28.3% from 25 to 44, 22.9% from 45 to 64, and 14.5% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 36 years.  For every 100 females there are 94.8 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 90.5 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $30,647, and the median income for a family is $34,542. Males have a median income of $26,118 versus $19,952 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $17,567.  20.1% of the population and 18.1% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 25.5% of those under the age of 18 and 27.9% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

