      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Bartlett''' is a city located in [[Shelby County, Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 40,543.

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-Bartlett.PNG|right|Location of Bartlett, Tennessee]]
Bartlett is located at 35&amp;deg;13'23&quot; North, 89&amp;deg;50'28&quot; West (35.222990, -89.841170){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 49.4 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (19.1 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  49.4 km&amp;sup2; (19.1 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.05% is water.

== Demographics ==
[[image:Bartlettseal.gif|right|thumb| Seal]]
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 40,543 people, 13,773 households, and 11,817 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 820.4/km&amp;sup2; (2,124.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 14,021 housing units at an average density of 283.7/km&amp;sup2; (734.7/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 92.44% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 4.86% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.28% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 1.24% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.04% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.37% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.77% from two or more races.  1.14% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 13,773 households out of which 44.0% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 74.6% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 8.7% have a female householder with no husband present, and 14.2% are non-families. 12.1% of all households are made up of individuals and 4.3% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.92 and the average family size is 3.18.

In the city the population is spread out with 29.1% under the age of 18, 6.8% from 18 to 24, 30.0% from 25 to 44, 25.5% from 45 to 64, and 8.6% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 37 years.  For every 100 females there are 95.4 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 91.2 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $66,369, and the median income for a family is $69,962. Males have a median income of $45,281 versus $32,382 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $24,616.  2.7% of the population and 2.1% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 3.2% of those under the age of 18 and 5.7% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

{{Tennessee}}

