      <comment>[[WP:AWB|AWB assisted]] category emptying per [[WP:CFD|CFD]] [[Wikipedia:Categories for deletion/Log/2006 January 14|Jan 14]]</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">:&lt;small&gt;''There are two other tiny places known as '''Germantown''' in Tennessee, see [[Germantown, Tennessee (disambiguation)]]''&lt;/small&gt;

'''Germantown''' is a city located in [[Shelby County, Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 37,348. 

Germantown is best known as a [[suburb]] of [[Memphis, Tennessee|Memphis]], [[Tennessee]].  Bordering Memphis to the east, Germantown is a quiet town of streets lined with mature hardwood trees, and often stately homes.  There is practically no industry in Germantown, but the city is home to significant, often high-end, retail.  In the city center is the Old Town Germantown neighborhood, anchored by a depot (a 1948 reproduction of the 1868 original) and railroad tracks that recall the community's earliest days of development as an outpost along the Memphis-Charleston Railroad.

Annual events in Germantown include the Germantown Festival, and the Germantown Charity Horse Show which lures equestrians from all over the country.

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-Germantown.PNG|right|Location of Germantown, Tennessee]]
Germantown is located at 35&amp;deg;5'20&quot; North, 89&amp;deg;47'38&quot; West (35.089023, -89.793997){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 45.6 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (17.6 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  45.5 km&amp;sup2; (17.6 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.1 km&amp;sup2; (0.04 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 0.17% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 37,348 people, 13,220 households, and 11,065 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 820.3/km&amp;sup2; (2,124.1/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 13,676 housing units at an average density of 300.4/km&amp;sup2; (777.8/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 92.94% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 2.33% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.16% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 3.50% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.03% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.17% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.87% from two or more races.  1.09% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 13,220 households out of which 41.2% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 75.7% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 6.1% have a female householder with no husband present, and 16.3% are non-families. 14.6% of all households are made up of individuals and 4.7% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.82 and the average family size is 3.14.

In the city the population is spread out with 28.0% under the age of 18, 5.8% from 18 to 24, 23.5% from 25 to 44, 33.5% from 45 to 64, and 9.2% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 41 years.  For every 100 females there are 95.0 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 92.2 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $94,609, and the median income for a family is $103,726. Males have a median income of $77,857 versus $38,311 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $44,021.  2.1% of the population and 1.6% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 2.0% of those under the age of 18 and 1.3% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

{{Tennessee}}

