      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Gordonsville''' is a town located in [[Smith County, Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 1,066.

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-Gordonsville.PNG|right|Location of Gordonsville, Tennessee]]
Gordonsville is located at 36&amp;deg;10'38&quot; North, 85&amp;deg;55'50&quot; West (36.177215, -85.930548){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 18.0 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (7.0 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  17.9 km&amp;sup2; (6.9 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.1 km&amp;sup2; (0.1 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 0.72% water.

