      <text xml:space="preserve">'''South Carthage''' is a town located in [[Smith County, Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 1,302.

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-SouthCarthage.PNG|right|Location of South Carthage, Tennessee]]
South Carthage is located at 36&amp;deg;14'44&quot; North, 85&amp;deg;57'29&quot; West (36.245584, -85.958043){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 6.9 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (2.7 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  6.7 km&amp;sup2; (2.6 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.2 km&amp;sup2; (0.1 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 2.99% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 1,302 people, 554 households, and 366 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 193.3/km&amp;sup2; (501.0/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 589 housing units at an average density of 87.5/km&amp;sup2; (226.6/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 95.31% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 2.46% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.08% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.23% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.54% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.38% from two or more races.  1.38% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 554 households out of which 33.0% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 50.2% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 12.8% have a female householder with no husband present, and 33.9% are non-families. 30.9% of all households are made up of individuals and 16.6% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.35 and the average family size is 2.92.

In the town the population is spread out with 25.4% under the age of 18, 7.1% from 18 to 24, 29.7% from 25 to 44, 21.4% from 45 to 64, and 16.4% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 37 years.  For every 100 females there are 86.0 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 79.8 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $30,592, and the median income for a family is $35,066. Males have a median income of $31,080 versus $20,577 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $14,425.  15.2% of the population and 10.7% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 14.6% of those under the age of 18 and 24.6% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== External links ==
{{Mapit-US-cityscale|36.245584|-85.958043}}

[[Category:Smith County, Tennessee]]
[[Category:Towns in Tennessee]]

[[io:South Carthage, Tennessee]]</text>
    </revision>
