      <text xml:space="preserve">[[Image:Tva powerplant.jpg|thumb|TVA Powerplant at Cumberland City]]
'''Cumberland City''' is a town located in [[Stewart County, Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 316.

Cumberland City is the site of a [[Tennessee Valley Authority|TVA]] [[power plant]] along the [[Cumberland River]] that provides power to much of the area, including the cities of [[Clarksville, Tennessee|Clarksville]] in [[Montgomery County, Tennessee|Montgomery County]] and [[Dickson, Tennessee|Dickson]] in [[Dickson County, Tennessee|Dickson County]].

The power plant's towers (some of the tallest structures in the state) can be seen for at least 30 miles away.

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-CumberlandCity.PNG|right|Location of Cumberland City, Tennessee]]
Cumberland City is located at 36&amp;deg;23'26&quot; North, 87&amp;deg;38'27&quot; West (36.390469, -87.640801){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 13.7 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (5.3 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  12.5 km&amp;sup2; (4.8 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 1.2 km&amp;sup2; (0.5 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 8.90% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 316 people, 139 households, and 89 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 25.4/km&amp;sup2; (65.6/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 178 housing units at an average density of 14.3/km&amp;sup2; (37.0/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 87.34% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 7.91% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.00% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.63% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 2.22% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.90% from two or more races.  2.22% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 139 households out of which 24.5% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 43.2% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 14.4% have a female householder with no husband present, and 35.3% are non-families. 29.5% of all households are made up of individuals and 17.3% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.27 and the average family size is 2.80.

In the town the population is spread out with 22.5% under the age of 18, 10.1% from 18 to 24, 23.4% from 25 to 44, 22.5% from 45 to 64, and 21.5% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 40 years.  For every 100 females there are 91.5 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 88.5 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $21,750, and the median income for a family is $26,250. Males have a median income of $31,875 versus $17,500 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $14,363.  27.3% of the population and 22.8% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 37.9% of those under the age of 18 and 23.8% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== External links ==
{{Mapit-US-cityscale|36.390469|-87.640801}}

[[Category:Stewart County, Tennessee]]
[[Category:Towns in Tennessee]]

[[io:Cumberland City, Tennessee]]</text>
    </revision>
