      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Dover''' is a city located in [[Stewart County, Tennessee]], 67 miles (108 km) westnorthwest of [[Nashville, Tennessee|Nashville]] on the [[Cumberland River]].  An old national cemetery is in Dover.  In [[1914]], the population was estimated at about 600 people.  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 1,442.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Stewart County, Tennessee|Stewart County]]{{GR|6}}.

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-Dover.PNG|right|Location of Dover, Tennessee]]Dover is located at 36&amp;deg;28'56&quot; North, 87&amp;deg;50'41&quot; West (36.482316, -87.844678){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 10.1 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (3.9 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  9.8 km&amp;sup2; (3.8 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.3 km&amp;sup2; (0.1 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 2.56% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 1,442 people, 608 households, and 373 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 146.5/km&amp;sup2; (379.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 656 housing units at an average density of 66.7/km&amp;sup2; (172.8/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 94.73% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 3.05% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.69% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.07% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.55% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.90% from two or more races.  0.83% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 608 households out of which 23.0% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 49.3% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 7.2% have a female householder with no husband present, and 38.5% are non-families. 36.3% of all households are made up of individuals and 21.7% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.21 and the average family size is 2.88.

In the city the population is spread out with 19.4% under the age of 18, 5.1% from 18 to 24, 24.2% from 25 to 44, 24.1% from 45 to 64, and 27.3% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 46 years.  For every 100 females there are 83.7 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 80.2 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $33,839, and the median income for a family is $42,266. Males have a median income of $27,227 versus $21,563 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $18,483.  11.1% of the population and 8.1% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 9.5% of those under the age of 18 and 16.7% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== External links ==
{{Mapit-US-cityscale|36.482316|-87.844678}}

[[Category:Cities in Tennessee]]
[[Category:Stewart County, Tennessee]]

[[io:Dover, Tennessee]]</text>
