      <comment>Kulwicki</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Blountville''' is a [[census-designated place]] located in [[Sullivan County, Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the CDP had a total population of 2,959.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Sullivan County, Tennessee|Sullivan County]]{{GR|6}} and is the only Tennessee county seat not to be an [[municipal corporation|incorporated]] city or town.  Despite its small size, Blountville is the home to the Tri-Cities Regional Airport primarily because of its central location between [[Johnson City, Tennessee|Johnson City]], [[Kingsport, Tennessee|Kingsport]], [[Bristol, Tennessee|Bristol, TN/VA]].  Boone Lake, a local summertime recreation area, is also located in the Blountville area. [[NASCAR]] champion [[Alan Kulwicki]] died in an airplane crash near Blountville.

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-Blountville.PNG|right|Location of Blountville, Tennessee]]
Blountville is located at 36&amp;deg;31'60&quot; North, 82&amp;deg;19'35&quot; West (36.533312, -82.326474){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the CDP has a total area of 14.8 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (5.7 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  14.8 km&amp;sup2; (5.7 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of the area is covered with water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 2,959 people, 1,060 households, and 763 families residing in the CDP.  The [[population density]] is 200.1/km&amp;sup2; (518.0/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 1,134 housing units at an average density of 76.7/km&amp;sup2; (198.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the CDP is 98.01% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 1.32% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.17% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.20% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.03% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.07% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.20% from two or more races.  0.88% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 1,060 households out of which 25.8% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 60.0% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 8.8% have a female householder with no husband present, and 28.0% are non-families. 25.8% of all households are made up of individuals and 11.3% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.36 and the average family size is 2.80.

In the CDP the population is spread out with 16.9% under the age of 18, 10.0% from 18 to 24, 35.3% from 25 to 44, 24.9% from 45 to 64, and 12.9% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 38 years.  For every 100 females there are 123.0 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 127.6 males.

The median income for a household in the CDP is $37,609, and the median income for a family is $41,594. Males have a median income of $31,842 versus $18,163 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the CDP is $16,173.  4.8% of the population and 3.0% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 1.4% of those under the age of 18 and 8.1% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== External links ==
{{Mapit-US-cityscale|36.533312|-82.326474}}

[[Category:Sullivan County, Tennessee]]
[[Category:Census-designated places in Tennessee]]</text>
