      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Walnut Hill''' is a [[census-designated place]] located in [[Sullivan County, Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the CDP had a total population of 2,756.

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-WalnutHill.PNG|right|Location of Walnut Hill, Tennessee]]
Walnut Hill is located at 36&amp;deg;34'17&quot; North, 82&amp;deg;15'28&quot; West (36.571440, -82.257832){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the CDP has a total area of 12.2 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (4.7 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  12.2 km&amp;sup2; (4.7 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of the area is covered with water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 2,756 people, 1,134 households, and 877 families residing in the CDP.  The [[population density]] is 225.9/km&amp;sup2; (585.3/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 1,176 housing units at an average density of 96.4/km&amp;sup2; (249.8/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the CDP is 98.51% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.51% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.25% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.29% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.00% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.44% from two or more races.  0.15% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 1,134 households out of which 27.9% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 67.2% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 7.3% have a female householder with no husband present, and 22.6% are non-families. 20.0% of all households are made up of individuals and 8.5% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.43 and the average family size is 2.78.

In the CDP the population is spread out with 19.6% under the age of 18, 5.8% from 18 to 24, 27.6% from 25 to 44, 30.8% from 45 to 64, and 16.1% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 43 years.  For every 100 females there are 95.5 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 94.6 males.

The median income for a household in the CDP is $39,677, and the median income for a family is $45,242. Males have a median income of $30,969 versus $23,659 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the CDP is $21,286.  8.5% of the population and 8.7% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 8.3% of those under the age of 18 and 13.3% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

