      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Munford''' is a town located in [[Tipton County, Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 4,708.

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-Munford.PNG|right|Location of Munford, Tennessee]]
Munford is located at 35&amp;deg;26'41&quot; North, 89&amp;deg;48'38&quot; West (35.444660, -89.810567){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 20.9 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (8.1 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  20.8 km&amp;sup2; (8.0 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.12% is water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 4,708 people, 1,674 households, and 1,334 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 226.1/km&amp;sup2; (585.4/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 1,735 housing units at an average density of 83.3/km&amp;sup2; (215.7/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 90.70% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 5.80% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.28% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.83% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.64% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.76% from two or more races.  1.51% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 1,674 households out of which 43.9% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 63.4% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 13.0% have a female householder with no husband present, and 20.3% are non-families. 17.1% of all households are made up of individuals and 6.6% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.81 and the average family size is 3.17.

In the town the population is spread out with 31.4% under the age of 18, 7.5% from 18 to 24, 30.3% from 25 to 44, 22.4% from 45 to 64, and 8.5% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 34 years.  For every 100 females there are 92.6 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 88.4 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $43,611, and the median income for a family is $46,406. Males have a median income of $40,200 versus $31,199 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $19,656.  13.3% of the population and 12.5% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 21.3% of those under the age of 18 and 8.6% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

