      <comment>/* Geography */</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''McMinnville''' is a city located in [[Warren County, Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 12,749.  The 2004 census estimate is 13,108, making McMinnville one of Tennessee's slowest growing cities.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Warren County, Tennessee|Warren County]]{{GR|6}}.  It was named after [[Joseph McMinn]], a governor of Tennessee.

Noted McMinnville natives include composer and musicologist [[Charles Faulkner Bryan]], country music singer [[Dottie West]], and US ambassador and political journalist [[Carl Rowan]].

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-McMinnville.PNG|right|Location of McMinnville, Tennessee]]
McMinnville is located at 35&amp;deg;41'12&quot; North, 85&amp;deg;46'46&quot; West (35.686708, -85.779309){{GR|1}}, approximately 35 miles south of [[Cookeville]] and 70 miles northwest of [[Chattanooga]].

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 25.9 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (10.0 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  25.9 km&amp;sup2; (10.0 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of the area is covered with water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 12,749 people, 5,419 households, and 3,332 families residing in the city.  The 2004 census estimate is 13,108.  The [[population density]] is 491.7/km&amp;sup2; (1,273.4/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 5,961 housing units at an average density of 229.9/km&amp;sup2; (595.4/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 88.42% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 4.15% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.16% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.93% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.05% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 5.00% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.28% from two or more races.  6.81% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 5,419 households out of which 28.6% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 42.6% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 14.8% have a female householder with no husband present, and 38.5% are non-families. 33.9% of all households are made up of individuals and 15.4% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.26 and the average family size is 2.86.

In the city the population is spread out with 23.5% under the age of 18, 10.1% from 18 to 24, 27.9% from 25 to 44, 20.6% from 45 to 64, and 18.0% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 36 years.  For every 100 females there are 87.3 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 84.0 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $23,810, and the median income for a family is $32,759. Males have a median income of $28,474 versus $20,693 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $15,074.  24.6% of the population and 21.0% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 34.5% of those under the age of 18 and 19.1% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

