      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Gray''' is a [[census-designated place]] located in [[Washington County, Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the CDP had a total population of 1,273.

Gray is an unincorporated [[suburb]] of [[Johnson City, Tennessee|Johnson City]], [[Johnson City, Tennessee|Tennessee]].  It lies just outside the junction between [[Interstate 81]] and [[Interstate 26]], the latter of which runs directly through the town.  Originally, the town was known as Gray Station, as it mainly served as a rail [[depot]], but over time, the shortened name became the preferred usage.  The Gray area consisted primarily of rural farmland until the late [[20th century]], when it began to grow and take shape as a mostly [[residential]] suburb, with some minor commercial activity.  

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-Gray.PNG|right|Location of Gray, Tennessee]]
Gray is located at 36&amp;deg;25'3&quot; North, 82&amp;deg;28'32&quot; West (36.417403, -82.475637){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the CDP has a total area of 4.4 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (1.7 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  4.4 km&amp;sup2; (1.7 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.60% is water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 1,273 people, 553 households, and 397 families residing in the CDP.  The [[population density]] is 292.6/km&amp;sup2; (758.7/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 586 housing units at an average density of 134.7/km&amp;sup2; (349.2/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the CDP is 98.35% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.55% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.24% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.31% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.39% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.16% from two or more races.  0.63% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 553 households out of which 30.0% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 57.3% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 12.1% have a female householder with no husband present, and 28.2% are non-families. 24.2% of all households are made up of individuals and 8.7% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.30 and the average family size is 2.73.

In the CDP the population is spread out with 21.6% under the age of 18, 7.9% from 18 to 24, 31.2% from 25 to 44, 23.5% from 45 to 64, and 15.9% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 38 years.  For every 100 females there are 87.5 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 86.5 males.

The median income for a household in the CDP is $30,469, and the median income for a family is $40,473. Males have a median income of $28,333 versus $18,750 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the CDP is $22,542.  14.3% of the population and 13.2% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 27.0% of those under the age of 18 and 12.3% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

