      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Sharon''' is a town located in [[Weakley County, Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 988.

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-Sharon.PNG|right|Location of Sharon, Tennessee]]
Sharon is located at 36&amp;deg;13'60&quot; North, 88&amp;deg;49'30&quot; West (36.233268, -88.825000){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 3.0 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (1.1 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  3.0 km&amp;sup2; (1.1 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of the area is covered with water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 988 people, 446 households, and 300 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 331.7/km&amp;sup2; (857.3/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 490 housing units at an average density of 164.5/km&amp;sup2; (425.2/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 89.17% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 10.22% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.00% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.00% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.10% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.40% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.10% from two or more races.  0.40% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 446 households out of which 23.3% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 55.6% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 9.2% have a female householder with no husband present, and 32.7% are non-families. 29.6% of all households are made up of individuals and 19.1% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.22 and the average family size is 2.73.

In the town the population is spread out with 19.4% under the age of 18, 6.4% from 18 to 24, 24.9% from 25 to 44, 26.8% from 45 to 64, and 22.5% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 44 years.  For every 100 females there are 93.7 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 87.7 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $27,639, and the median income for a family is $39,643. Males have a median income of $29,018 versus $17,708 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $15,746.  12.7% of the population and 11.3% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 15.3% of those under the age of 18 and 16.0% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

