      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Sparta''' is a city located in [[White County, Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 4,599.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[White County, Tennessee|White County]]{{GR|6}}.  It was the hometown of [[Lester Flatt]] of the [[bluegrass music]] legends [[Flatt and Scruggs]]. 

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-Sparta.PNG|right|Location of Sparta, Tennessee]]
Sparta is located at 35&amp;deg;55'56&quot; North, 85&amp;deg;28'11&quot; West (35.932335, -85.469837){{GR|1}}, approximately 15 miles south of [[Cookeville]].

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 16.4 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (6.3 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  16.4 km&amp;sup2; (6.3 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of the area is covered with water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 4,599 people, 1,952 households, and 1,270 families residing in the city. A special census was later conducted by the City of Sparta in 2001 making the official population at 5,030. The [[population density]] is 280.1/km&amp;sup2; (725.2/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 2,192 housing units at an average density of 133.5/km&amp;sup2; (345.7/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 91.82% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 5.28% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.20% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.65% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.13% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.67% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.24% from two or more races.  1.15% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 1,952 households out of which 27.6% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 43.7% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 17.6% have a female householder with no husband present, and 34.9% are non-families. 32.8% of all households are made up of individuals and 17.9% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.24 and the average family size is 2.81.

In the city the population is spread out with 21.8% under the age of 18, 7.7% from 18 to 24, 25.0% from 25 to 44, 22.9% from 45 to 64, and 22.5% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 41 years.  For every 100 females there are 85.1 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 77.7 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $23,775, and the median income for a family is $33,060. Males have a median income of $26,970 versus $20,295 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $15,340.  21.3% of the population and 16.2% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 30.3% of those under the age of 18 and 14.3% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

==Local Government==

Governing Body:
Mayor — Tommy L. Pedigo;
Vice Mayor — Hoyt Jones; 
Alderman — Howard Griffin; 
Alderman — Ben Holland; 
Alderman — Robert Officer; 
Alderman — Margaret Pearson; 
Alderman — Debbie Sopha 

Staff:
City Administrator — Marty Carmichael;
City Court Clerk — Lorie Spivey;
City Judge — William D. Mitchell; 
City Recorder — Tonya R. Tindle; 
Code Enforcement Officer — Dennis Clark; 
Fire Chief — Eddie Kay; 
Police Chief — Jeff Guth,
Accounts Payable — Angie Wilhite; 
Street/Sanitation Superintendent — Clay Parker; 
Utility Manager — Wayne Rogers; 
Water/Sewer Superintendent — Bill Klein; 
Electric Superintendent — Gary McCulley;
City Attorney — Lynn Omohundro

