      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Brentwood''' is a city located in [[Williamson County, Tennessee]], [[USA]]. As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 23,445. Brentwood is known as an affluent suburb of Nashville.

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-Brentwood.PNG|right|Location of Brentwood, Tennessee]]
Brentwood is located at 35&amp;deg;59'53&quot; North, 86&amp;deg;47'33&quot; West (35.998194, -86.792619)[[Geographic references|&lt;sup&gt;1&lt;/sup&gt;]].

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 89.8 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (34.7 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  89.7 km&amp;sup2; (34.7 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.1 km&amp;sup2; (0.04 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 0.06% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 23,445 people, 7,693 households, and 6,808 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 261.2/km&amp;sup2; (676.7/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 7,889 housing units at an average density of 87.9/km&amp;sup2; (227.7/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 94.63% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 1.89% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.16% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 2.50% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.19% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.64% from two or more races.  1.10% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 7,693 households out of which 48.2% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 82.2% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 4.9% have a female householder with no husband present, and 11.5% are non-families. 10.0% of all households are made up of individuals and 3.2% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 3.02 and the average family size is 3.24.

In the city the population is spread out with 31.5% under the age of 18, 4.3% from 18 to 24, 23.6% from 25 to 44, 32.4% from 45 to 64, and 8.2% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 41 years.  For every 100 females there are 97.1 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 93.2 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $111,819, and the median income for a family is $118,450. Males have a median income of $97,962 versus $41,324 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $47,378.  2.0% of the population and 1.5% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 2.5% of those under the age of 18 and 4.5% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== Famous residents ==
Brentwood is the home of former [[NASCAR]] driver [[Casey Atwood]], and several musicians, including [[Trisha Yearwood]], [[Dolly Parton]], [[George Jones]], [[Little Jimmy Dickens]], and [[Alan Jackson]].  Brentwood is also the former home of [[Peter Frampton]].


{{Tennessee}}

