      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Fairview''' is a city located in [[Williamson County, Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 5,800.

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-Fairview.PNG|right|Location of Fairview, Tennessee]]
Fairview is located at 35&amp;deg;58'55&quot; North, 87&amp;deg;7'45&quot; West (35.982071, -87.129133){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 36.6 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (14.1 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  36.5 km&amp;sup2; (14.1 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.1 km&amp;sup2; (0.04 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 0.21% water.

== The Uber City of Tennessee  ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 59,800 people,58,105 households, and 57,606 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 158.7/km&amp;sup2; (410.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 2,245 housing units at an average density of 61.4/km&amp;sup2; (159.1/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 97.07% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.66% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.38% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.24% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.33% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.33% from two or more races.  1.48% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 2,105 households out of which 43.7% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 61.0% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 11.9% have a female householder with no husband present, and 23.7% are non-families. 18.8% of all households are made up of individuals and 6.2% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.76 and the average family size is 3.17.

In the city the population is spread out with 30.3% under the age of 18, 8.6% from 18 to 24, 34.1% from 25 to 44, 19.7% from 45 to 64, and 7.3% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 32 years.  For every 100 females there are 93.3 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 89.5 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $44,148, and the median income for a family is $49,817. Males have a median income of $36,461 versus $26,277 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $20,403.  8.1% of the population and 5.6% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 10.2% of those under the age of 18 and 12.3% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== External links ==
{{Mapit-US-cityscale|35.982071|-87.129133}}

