  <page>
    <title>Franklin, Tennessee</title>
    <id>135422</id>
    <revision>
      <id>40639856</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-22T00:18:44Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>All in</username>
        <id>605330</id>
      </contributor>
      <comment>/* External links */ formatting</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Franklin''' is a city located in [[Williamson County, Tennessee]], [[United States|USA]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 41,842.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Williamson County, Tennessee|Williamson County]]{{GR|6}}. 

== History ==

The City of Franklin was founded October 26, 1799 and was named after [[Benjamin Franklin]], a close friend of Dr. [[Hugh Williamson]], a member of the [[Continental Congress]] for whom Williamson County was named. 

For most of its first 180 years, Franklin was a tranquil, small county seat. In the years prior to the [[American Civil War]], Williamson County was one of the wealthiest counties in Tennessee and Franklin was the center of plantation economy. 

However, the Civil War devastated the economy. [[Union (American Civil War)|Union]] troops occupied the area for nearly three years. The [[Battle of Franklin]] was fought on November 30, 1864, costing more than 8,000 casualties and turning every home and building in town into a hospital. It took 120 years for the county's economy to reach pre-war levels. 

For more than a century, Franklin seemed remote not only from [[Nashville, Tennessee]], but from the rest of the world as well. Today, Franklin is one of the wealthiest cities in one of the wealthiest counties in the United States. . 

Franklin has grown from a very small, agricultural community into a strong blend of residential, commercial and corporate citizens.


== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-Franklin.PNG|right|Location of Franklin, Tennessee]]
Franklin is located at 35&amp;deg;55'45&quot; North, 86&amp;deg;51'27&quot; West (35.929074, -86.857402){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 78.0 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (30.1 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  77.8 km&amp;sup2; (30.0 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.2 km&amp;sup2; (0.1 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 0.27% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 41,842 people, 16,128 households, and 11,225 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 538.0/km&amp;sup2; (1,393.3/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 17,296 housing units at an average density of 222.4/km&amp;sup2; (575.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 84.53% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 10.35% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.24% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 1.61% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.05% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 2.17% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.06% from two or more races.  4.84% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 16,128 households out of which 38.6% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 56.2% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 10.8% have a female householder with no husband present, and 30.4% are non-families. 25.0% of all households are made up of individuals and 5.4% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.55 and the average family size is 3.09.

In the city the population is spread out with 27.9% under the age of 18, 7.5% from 18 to 24, 38.1% from 25 to 44, 19.2% from 45 to 64, and 7.4% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 33 years.  For every 100 females there are 93.6 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 90.2 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $56,431, and the median income for a family is $69,431. Males have a median income of $50,226 versus $31,531 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $27,276.  6.7% of the population and 5.1% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 8.0% of those under the age of 18 and 12.0% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

The 2004 Special Census lists the city's population at just over 46,000 making it the 10th largest city in the state and the fastest growing.

== Trivia ==
*Franklin is the home of retired [[NASCAR]] driver [[Darrell Waltrip]], who also owns a car dealership there. It is also the home of country singer [[Josh Gracin]], ''[[American Idol]]'' 2 finalist and musician [[Lee Greenwood]], and professional wrestler [[James Storm]], who currently wrestles for [[Total Nonstop Action Wrestling]].
*[[Big Idea Productions]], creators of [[Veggie Tales]] is located in Franklin.
*The band, [[Paramore]], was formed here.

==See also==
*[[Battle of Franklin]]

{{Tennessee}}

