      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Thompson's Station''' is a town located in [[Williamson County, Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 1,283.

== Geography ==
Thompson's Station is located at 35&amp;deg;47'55&quot; North, 86&amp;deg;54'26&quot; West (35.798670, -86.907341){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 38.1 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (14.7 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  38.1 km&amp;sup2; (14.7 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of the area is covered with water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 1,283 people, 447 households, and 375 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 33.7/km&amp;sup2; (87.2/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 473 housing units at an average density of 12.4/km&amp;sup2; (32.2/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 91.19% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 7.01% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.16% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.55% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.62% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 0.47% from two or more races.  2.57% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 447 households out of which 40.0% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 75.2% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 6.9% have a female householder with no husband present, and 15.9% are non-families. 14.1% of all households are made up of individuals and 4.7% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.87 and the average family size is 3.17.

In the town the population is spread out with 26.8% under the age of 18, 6.3% from 18 to 24, 31.0% from 25 to 44, 26.8% from 45 to 64, and 9.0% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 38 years.  For every 100 females there are 102.4 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 96.4 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $66,875, and the median income for a family is $70,568. Males have a median income of $50,337 versus $31,528 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $24,143.  4.4% of the population and 4.1% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 5.3% of those under the age of 18 and 12.6% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

