      <text xml:space="preserve">''This page is about a real location. For the Sonic The Hedgehog videogame stage, see [[Green Hill Zone]].''

'''Green Hill''' is a [[census-designated place]] located in [[Wilson County, Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the CDP had a total population of 7,068.

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-GreenHill.PNG|right|Location of Green Hill, Tennessee]]
Green Hill is located at 36&amp;deg;13'51&quot; North, 86&amp;deg;34'25&quot; West (36.230879, -86.573623){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the CDP has a total area of 11.4 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (4.4 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  10.1 km&amp;sup2; (3.9 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 1.3 km&amp;sup2; (0.5 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 11.59% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 7,068 people, 2,555 households, and 2,141 families residing in the CDP.  The [[population density]] is 701.5/km&amp;sup2; (1,815.7/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 2,613 housing units at an average density of 259.4/km&amp;sup2; (671.3/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the CDP is 94.57% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 3.03% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.16% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.72% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.03% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.31% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.19% from two or more races.  0.96% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 2,555 households out of which 37.3% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 72.6% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 8.5% have a female householder with no husband present, and 16.2% are non-families. 13.0% of all households are made up of individuals and 3.4% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.77 and the average family size is 3.02.

In the CDP the population is spread out with 25.6% under the age of 18, 6.7% from 18 to 24, 28.3% from 25 to 44, 31.4% from 45 to 64, and 8.0% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 40 years.  For every 100 females there are 100.1 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 96.5 males.

The median income for a household in the CDP is $62,690, and the median income for a family is $66,610. Males have a median income of $45,931 versus $31,237 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the CDP is $25,926.  3.4% of the population and 2.4% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 6.1% of those under the age of 18 and 0.9% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

Green Hill is not to be confused with the Nashville [[suburb]] of [[Green Hills, Tennessee|Green Hills]] in [[Davidson County, Tennessee|Davidson County]].

== External links ==
