      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Rural Hill''' is an unincorporated [[census-designated place]] located in [[Wilson County, Tennessee|Wilson County]], [[Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the community had a total population of 2,032.

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-RuralHill.PNG|right|Location of Rural Hill, Tennessee]]
Rural Hill is located at 36&amp;deg;7'7&quot; North, 86&amp;deg;31'8&quot; West (36.118696, -86.518771){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the community has a total area of 10.0 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (3.9 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  10.0 km&amp;sup2; (3.8 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.1 km&amp;sup2; (0.04 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 0.77% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 2,032 people, 689 households, and 622 families residing in the community.  The [[population density]] is 203.8/km&amp;sup2; (527.7/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 697 housing units at an average density of 69.9/km&amp;sup2; (181.0/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the community is 96.16% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 1.38% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.10% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.69% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.10% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.34% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.23% from two or more races.  1.72% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 689 households out of which 44.6% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 84.2% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 4.2% have a female householder with no husband present, and 9.7% are non-families. 6.7% of all households are made up of individuals and 2.3% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.95 and the average family size is 3.10.

The population is spread out with 28.6% under the age of 18, 4.4% from 18 to 24, 34.2% from 25 to 44, 26.9% from 45 to 64, and 5.9% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 38 years.  For every 100 females there are 103.6 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 98.2 males.

The median income for a household in the community is $80,346, and the median income for a family is $83,005. Males have a median income of $54,348 versus $31,848 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the community is $28,571.  0.5% of the population and 0.0% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 0.0% of those under the age of 18 and 5.6% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== External links ==
{{Mapit-US-cityscale|36.118696|-86.518771}}

