      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Watertown''' is a city located in [[Wilson County, Tennessee]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 1,358.

== Geography ==
[[Image:TNMap-doton-Watertown.PNG|right|Location of Watertown, Tennessee]]
Watertown is located at 36&amp;deg;6'0&quot; North, 86&amp;deg;8'14&quot; West (36.100039, -86.137102){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 3.2 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (1.2 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  3.2 km&amp;sup2; (1.2 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of the area is covered with water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 1,358 people, 542 households, and 377 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 419.5/km&amp;sup2; (1,083.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 605 housing units at an average density of 186.9/km&amp;sup2; (482.9/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 91.24% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 6.11% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.37% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.07% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.66% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.55% from two or more races.  1.25% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 542 households out of which 33.4% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 51.5% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 13.3% have a female householder with no husband present, and 30.3% are non-families. 28.4% of all households are made up of individuals and 14.6% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.51 and the average family size is 3.06.

In the city the population is spread out with 26.7% under the age of 18, 8.5% from 18 to 24, 28.3% from 25 to 44, 21.2% from 45 to 64, and 15.4% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 37 years.  For every 100 females there are 89.7 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 82.8 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $35,662, and the median income for a family is $41,484. Males have a median income of $30,263 versus $22,500 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $17,008.  11.0% of the population and 9.2% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 15.2% of those under the age of 18 and 8.5% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== Arts and Entertainment ==
*In 1997, songwriter [[Tom T. Hall]] immortalized the city in a song titled appropriately, ''Watertown, Tennessee'', which still receives occasional radio airplay on country stations. 
*Country singer [[Garth Brooks]] filmed a [[Dr Pepper]] television commercial and his &quot;Wrapped Up In You&quot; music video on the town square in 2001.
*In 2003, a new [[Drive-in theater]] successfully opened in Watertown, a very unusual event since most drive-ins around the country have closed.
*The city is a frequent destination of excursion trains from nearby [[Nashville|Nashville, Tennessee]] run by the [[Tennessee Central Railway Museum]].

== External links ==
*[http://www.watertowntn.com/ Official city site]
*[http://www.songlyricscollection.com/t/Tom%20T%20Hall/Home%20Grown/Watertown%20Tennessee%20lyrics.htm Watertown song lyrics]
*[http://www.stardustdrivein.com/ Stardust Drive-In]
{{Geolinks-US-cityscale|36.100039|-86.137102}}

