      <comment>/* Noted natives */</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Frankston''' is a town located in [[Anderson County, Texas]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 1,209. Frankston was named for [[Frankie Miller]], a young woman who donated land for the downtown city park.

== Geography ==
[[Image:TXMap-doton-Frankston.PNG|right|Location of Frankston, Texas]]
Frankston is located at 32&amp;deg;3'14&quot; North, 95&amp;deg;30'24&quot; West (32.053827, -95.506528){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 6.4 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (2.5 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  6.4 km&amp;sup2; (2.5 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of the area is covered with water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 1,209 people, 472 households, and 320 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 189.0/km&amp;sup2; (488.6/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 525 housing units at an average density of 82.1/km&amp;sup2; (212.2/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 86.68% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 10.92% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.17% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.08% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 0.91% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.24% from two or more races.  2.81% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 472 households out of which 28.8% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 53.4% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 11.9% have a female householder with no husband present, and 32.2% are non-families. 29.9% of all households are made up of individuals and 21.2% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.44 and the average family size is 3.02.

In the town the population is spread out with 23.1% under the age of 18, 6.9% from 18 to 24, 21.9% from 25 to 44, 23.7% from 45 to 64, and 24.3% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 44 years.  For every 100 females there are 80.4 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 72.5 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $28,125, and the median income for a family is $37,130. Males have a median income of $27,250 versus $20,313 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $15,609.  17.1% of the population and 12.8% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 14.0% of those under the age of 18 and 25.6% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

==Noted natives==
*[[Frank Beard (musician)]]-Drummer for [[ZZ Top]] and only beardless member.

== External links ==
{{Mapit-US-cityscale|32.053827|-95.506528}}

[[Category:Anderson County, Texas]]
[[Category:Towns in Texas]]</text>
