      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Lufkin''' is a city located in [[Angelina County, Texas]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 32,709.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Angelina County, Texas|Angelina County]]{{GR|6}}, and is situated in [[East Texas]]. The town is named for [[Abraham P. Lufkin]], a [[cotton]] merchant and [[Galveston, Texas]] city councilman. Lufkin was the son-in-law of [[Paul Bremond]], president of the [[Houston, East and West Texas Railway]] which developed the town.

Founded in [[1882]], Lufkin is home to [[Lufkin Industries]], which manufactures and services oil field equipment, power transmissions, and highway trailers. It is also a leading supplier of [[creosote]].

== Geography ==
[[Image:TXMap-doton-Lufkin.PNG|right|Location of Lufkin, Texas]]
Lufkin is located at 31&amp;deg;20'13&quot; North, 94&amp;deg;43'49&quot; West (31.336874, -94.730374){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 69.5 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (26.8 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  69.2 km&amp;sup2; (26.7 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.3 km&amp;sup2; (0.1 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 0.48% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 32,709 people, 12,247 households, and 8,364 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 473.0/km&amp;sup2; (1,225.1/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 13,402 housing units at an average density of 193.8/km&amp;sup2; (502.0/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 59.92% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 26.58% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.26% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 1.38% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.02% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 10.31% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.54% from two or more races.  17.59% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 12,247 households out of which 32.9% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 49.4% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 14.7% have a female householder with no husband present, and 31.7% are non-families. 27.9% of all households are made up of individuals and 11.9% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.58 and the average family size is 3.17.

In the city the population is spread out with 27.0% under the age of 18, 10.6% from 18 to 24, 27.3% from 25 to 44, 20.1% from 45 to 64, and 15.1% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 34 years.  For every 100 females there are 88.9 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 84.5 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $32,989, and the median income for a family is $40,591. Males have a median income of $30,922 versus $20,008 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $17,613.  18.8% of the population and 15.0% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 26.4% of those under the age of 18 and 12.6% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== Transportation ==
Lufkin is served by the following [[U.S. Highways]]: [[U.S. Route 69|U.S. 69]] and [[U.S. Route 59|U.S. 59]].

General Aviation service is provided by [[Angelina County Airport]].

== External links ==
