      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Bellville''' is a city located in [[Austin County, Texas]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the city had a total population of 3,794.  It is the [[county seat]] of [[Austin County, Texas|Austin County]]{{GR|6}}.

== Geography ==
[[Image:TXMap-doton-Bellville.PNG|right|Location of Bellville, Texas]]
Bellville is located at 29&amp;deg;56'50&quot; North, 96&amp;deg;15'31&quot; West (29.947225, -96.258657){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 6.8 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (2.6 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  6.8 km&amp;sup2; (2.6 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and none of the area is covered with water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 3,794 people, 1,425 households, and 966 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 561.3/km&amp;sup2; (1,452.0/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 1,566 housing units at an average density of 231.7/km&amp;sup2; (599.3/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 81.89% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 11.68% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.40% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.34% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 3.95% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.74% from two or more races.  11.97% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 1,425 households out of which 34.7% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 52.6% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 11.6% have a female householder with no husband present, and 32.2% are non-families. 27.9% of all households are made up of individuals and 15.3% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.52 and the average family size is 3.11.

In the city the population is spread out with 26.4% under the age of 18, 8.3% from 18 to 24, 25.3% from 25 to 44, 20.2% from 45 to 64, and 19.7% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 38 years.  For every 100 females there are 90.9 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 85.1 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $40,806, and the median income for a family is $49,730. Males have a median income of $36,719 versus $21,685 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $17,671.  8.0% of the population and 4.5% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 7.9% of those under the age of 18 and 8.1% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== Education ==
[[Bellville Independent School District]] serves Bellville.
=== Schools ===
* Bellville High School (Grades 9-12)
* Bellville Junior High School (Grades 6-8)
* O'Bryant Intermediate School (4-5)
* O'Bryant Primary School (PK-3)
* West End Elementary School (K-5)
* Faith Academy (Private school)

