      <text xml:space="preserve">'''San Felipe''' is a town located in [[Austin County, Texas]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the town had a total population of 868.

== Geography ==
[[Image:TXMap-doton-SanFelipe.PNG|right|Location of San Felipe, Texas]]
San Felipe is located at 29&amp;deg;47'40&quot; North, 96&amp;deg;6'17&quot; West (29.794442, -96.104612){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the town has a total area of 22.4 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (8.6 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  21.7 km&amp;sup2; (8.4 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.7 km&amp;sup2; (0.3 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 3.12% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 868 people, 312 households, and 234 families residing in the town.  The [[population density]] is 40.0/km&amp;sup2; (103.7/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 347 housing units at an average density of 16.0/km&amp;sup2; (41.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the town is 60.83% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 34.56% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.35% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.00% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 3.00% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.27% from two or more races.  9.45% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 312 households out of which 29.8% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 57.7% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 13.5% have a female householder with no husband present, and 24.7% are non-families. 23.1% of all households are made up of individuals and 8.3% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.78 and the average family size is 3.26.

In the town the population is spread out with 27.8% under the age of 18, 8.1% from 18 to 24, 22.9% from 25 to 44, 27.0% from 45 to 64, and 14.3% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 39 years.  For every 100 females there are 102.3 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 92.3 males.

The median income for a household in the town is $38,203, and the median income for a family is $43,558. Males have a median income of $31,667 versus $22,500 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the town is $17,169.  9.1% of the population and 9.1% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 3.1% of those under the age of 18 and 16.0% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

