      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Sealy''' is located in the U.S. state of Texas within the [[Houston-Sugar Land-Baytown Metropolitan Area]].  Sealy is located in [[Austin County, Texas]].  As of the [[2004]] census, the city had a total population of 5,563.

== Geography ==
[[Image:TXMap-doton-Sealy.PNG|right|Location of Sealy, Texas]]
Sealy is located at 29&amp;deg;46'27&quot; North, 96&amp;deg;9'27&quot; West (29.774182, -96.157570){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the city has a total area of 17.9 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (6.9 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  17.9 km&amp;sup2; (6.9 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 0.1 km&amp;sup2; (0.04 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 0.29% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2004]], there are 5,563 people, 1,882 households, and 1,349 families residing in the city.  The [[population density]] is 293.2/km&amp;sup2; (759.3/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 2,077 housing units at an average density of 116.1/km&amp;sup2; (300.5/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the city is 71.51% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 12.82% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.30% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.55% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.00% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 12.88% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.92% from two or more races.  30.43% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 1,882 households out of which 38.4% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 52.6% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 13.7% have a female householder with no husband present, and 28.3% are non-families. 24.5% of all households are made up of individuals and 11.7% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.75 and the average family size is 3.30.

In the city the population is spread out with 30.2% under the age of 18, 9.3% from 18 to 24, 28.9% from 25 to 44, 19.2% from 45 to 64, and 12.5% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 33 years.  For every 100 females there are 91.3 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 87.8 males.

The median income for a household in the city is $34,277, and the median income for a family is $40,348. Males have a median income of $28,720 versus $20,793 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the city is $15,986.  15.6% of the population and 11.2% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 18.9% of those under the age of 18 and 13.5% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

== Education ==
Pupils in Sealy are zoned to schools in [[Sealy Independent School District]]. The schools in Sealy ISD are Selman Elementary School (Pre-Kindergarten to second grade), Selman Intermediate School (3-5), Sealy Junior High School (6-8), and Sealy High School (9-12). All of the schools are in Sealy.  Blinn College also serves Sealy now, at the Sealy Mall.

