      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Lakehills''' is a [[census-designated place]] located in [[Bandera County, Texas]].  As of the [[2000]] census, the CDP had a total population of 4,668.

== Geography ==
[[Image:TXMap-doton-Lakehills.PNG|right|Location of Lakehills, Texas]]
Lakehills is located at 29&amp;deg;35'51&quot; North, 98&amp;deg;56'48&quot; West (29.597381, -98.946606){{GR|1}}.

According to the [[United States Census Bureau]], the CDP has a total area of 89.0 [[square kilometer|km&amp;sup2;]] (34.4 [[square mile|mi&amp;sup2;]]).  78.5 km&amp;sup2; (30.3 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is land and 10.6 km&amp;sup2; (4.1 mi&amp;sup2;) of it is water.  The total area is 11.87% water.

== Demographics ==
As of the [[census]]{{GR|2}} of [[2000]], there are 4,668 people, 1,874 households, and 1,330 families residing in the CDP.  The [[population density]] is 59.5/km&amp;sup2; (154.1/mi&amp;sup2;).  There are 2,807 housing units at an average density of 35.8/km&amp;sup2; (92.7/mi&amp;sup2;).  The racial makeup of the CDP is 93.04% [[White (U.S. Census)|White]], 0.43% [[African American (U.S. Census)|African American]], 0.75% [[Native American (U.S. Census)|Native American]], 0.28% [[Asian (U.S. Census)|Asian]], 0.06% [[Pacific Islander (U.S. Census)|Pacific Islander]], 3.58% from [[Race (U.S. Census)|other races]], and 1.86% from two or more races.  12.90% of the population are [[Hispanic (U.S. Census)|Hispanic]] or [[Latino (U.S. Census)|Latino]] of any race.

There are 1,874 households out of which 29.3% have children under the age of 18 living with them, 59.9% are [[Marriage|married couples]] living together, 6.6% have a female householder with no husband present, and 29.0% are non-families. 22.8% of all households are made up of individuals and 8.6% have someone living alone who is 65 years of age or older.  The average household size is 2.49 and the average family size is 2.92.

In the CDP the population is spread out with 24.6% under the age of 18, 5.4% from 18 to 24, 28.2% from 25 to 44, 27.9% from 45 to 64, and 13.9% who are 65 years of age or older.  The median age is 41 years.  For every 100 females there are 100.5 males.  For every 100 females age 18 and over, there are 101.5 males.

The median income for a household in the CDP is $42,964, and the median income for a family is $49,464. Males have a median income of $32,444 versus $26,158 for females. The [[per capita income]] for the CDP is $21,100.  10.5% of the population and 7.8% of families are below the [[poverty line]].  Out of the total population, 16.9% of those under the age of 18 and 3.6% of those 65 and older are living below the poverty line.

